<Base title="About EBT Places" desc="What EBT Places is, where the restaurant data comes from, and why we are not the USDA.">
<main class="wrap">
  <h1 style="font-size:1.6rem">About EBT Places</h1>
  <p class="lede">EBT Places is a <strong>private, independent</strong> guide to restaurants that accept EBT through the SNAP Restaurant Meals Program (RMP). We are not affiliated with the USDA, the Food and Nutrition Administration, or any state agency.</p>
  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <p>We organize the USDA's public SNAP Retailer Locator data — specifically the restaurants authorized for the Restaurant Meals Program — into pages by state, city and chain, so eligible recipients can find a hot meal quickly. Everything is free and we never ask for personal information.</p>
  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Enroll anyone in SNAP or RMP — only your state agency can.</li>
    <li>Confirm your personal eligibility — your state SNAP office does that.</li>
    <li>Guarantee a location still accepts EBT — always confirm with the restaurant.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Sources</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Restaurant locations:</strong> USDA SNAP Retailer Locator (authorized Restaurant Meals Program stores), refreshed periodically.</li>
    <li><strong>Program rules:</strong> USDA FNA SNAP regulations and state RMP documentation.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Funding</h2>
  <p>The site is supported by advertising, clearly separated from content.</p>
</main>
</Base>
